          %h2#ideas Ideas
          %p
            %em Mayer-Vietoris sequence
            is the term for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+sequence"} fiber sequence
            – or often for the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence+of+homotopy+groups"} long exact sequence of homotopy groups
            – induced from an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
            (or for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            presenting it).
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limits"} finite (∞,1)-limits
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y, B
            be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+objects"} pointed objects
            and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f : X \to B
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g : Y \to B
          %p
            be any two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            with common
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
            preserving the base points. Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times_B Y
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mi B
                          %mi Y
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi g
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  X \times_B Y &amp;\to&amp; Y
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;\swArrow_\simeq&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{g}}
                  \\\
                  X &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; B
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            The corresponding
            %strong Mayer-Vietoris sequence
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+sequence"} fiber sequence
            of the induced morphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times_B Y \to X \times Y
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence+of+homotopy+groups"} long exact sequence of homotopy groups
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#GeneralProperties General
          #SequenceFromDiagonal.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentable (∞,1)-category
            %p
              Then
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi B
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times_B Y
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi B
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ⇙
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi g
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X \times_B Y &amp;\to&amp; Y
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;\swArrow_{\simeq}&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{g}}
                    \\\
                    X  &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; B
                    }
            %p
              is equivalently also the following
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi B
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ⇙
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi Δ
                                    %mi B
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi f
                                %mo ,
                                %mi g
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                            %mo ×
                            %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X \times_B Y &amp;\to&amp; B
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;\swArrow_{\simeq}&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\Delta_B}}
                    \\\
                    X \times Y &amp;\stackrel{(f,g)}{\to}&amp; B \times B
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the right vertical morphism is the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal"} diagonal
            %p
              Moreover, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times_B Y \to X \times Y
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega B
          %p
            See also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "homotopy+pullback#HomotopyPullbackByFactorizationLemma"} this corollary
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The first statement one checks for instance by choosing a presentation by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
              and then proceeding as below in the discussion
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#PresentationByFibrantObjects"} Presentation by fibrant objects
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
              for
              = succeed "-pullbacks" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi B
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ⇙
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ⇙
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi f
                                %mo ,
                                %mi g
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                            %mo ×
                            %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\Omega B &amp;\to&amp; X \times_B Y &amp;\to &amp; B
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;\swArrow_{\simeq}&amp; \downarrow &amp;\swArrow_{\simeq}&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    * &amp;\to&amp; X \times Y &amp;\stackrel{(f,g)}{\to}&amp; B \times B
                    }
            %p
              an
              = succeed "-pullback," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "-pullback" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ⇙
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\Omega B &amp;\to&amp; *
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;\swArrow_{\simeq}&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    * &amp;\to&amp; B
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              which is the defining pullback for the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
          %p
            Therefore the Mayer-Vietoris
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+sequence"} homotopy fiber sequence
            is of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega B \to X \times_B Y \to X \times Y
                  \\,.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi whe
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \simeq L_{whe}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#DyerRoitberg80"} Dyer-Roitberg 80
          #LongExactSequenceOfHomotopyGroups.num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              The corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence+of+homotopy+groups"} long exact sequence of homotopy groups
              is of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mi Y
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots \to \pi_{n+1} B \to \pi_n (X \times_B Y) \stackrel{(f_*, g_*)}{\to} \pi_n X \oplus \pi_n Y \stackrel{f_* - g_*}{\to} \pi_n B \to \cdots
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 2
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mi Y
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msubsup
                          %mi g
                          %mo *
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots \to \pi_2 B \to \pi_1 (X \times_B Y) \stackrel{(f_*, g_*)}{\to}  \pi_1 X \times \pi_1 Y \stackrel{f_* \cdot g_*^{-1}}{\to} \pi_1 B \to \pi_0 (X \times_B Y) \to \pi_0 (X \times Y)
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is what has historically been the definition of Mayer-Vietoris sequences (
            %a{:href => "#EckmannHilton"}> Eckmann-Hilton 64
            ).
          %h3#PresentationByFibrantObjects Presentation by fibrant objects
          %p
            Suppose that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} presented
            by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            (for instance the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
            on the fibrant objects of a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
          %p
            Then the
            = succeed "-pullback" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times_B Y
            is presented by a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+lemma"} factorization lemma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                          %msubsup
                            %mo ×
                            %mi B
                            %mi h
                          %mi Y
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi g
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi B
                            %mi I
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  X \times^h_B Y &amp;\to&amp; &amp;\to&amp; Y
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{g}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; B^I &amp;\to&amp; B
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  X &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; B
                  }
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mo ×
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} B^I \to B \times B
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+object"} path object
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                          %msubsup
                            %mo ×
                            %mi B
                            %mi h
                          %mi Y
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi B
                            %mi I
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                          %mo ×
                          %mi Y
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi f
                              %mo ,
                              %mi g
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                          %mo ×
                          %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  X \times_B^h Y &amp;\to&amp; B^I
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  X \times Y &amp;\stackrel{(f,g)}{\to}&amp; B \times B
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            This implies in particular that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                    %mi h
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times_B^h Y \to X \times Y
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+space+object"} path space object
            projection.
          %h3#OverAGroupObject
            Over an
            = succeed "-group" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            We consider now the case where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            carries the structure of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            (or just a grouplike
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-space"} H-space
            object) in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentable (∞,1)-category
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+Cartesian+closed+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} locally Cartesian closed (∞,1)-category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          %p
            In this case (as discussed in a moment), we have an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi Δ
                                  %mi B
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi e
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                          %mo ×
                          %mi B
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ⋅
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  B &amp;\to&amp; *
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\Delta_B}}
                  \&amp;\swArrow_{\simeq}&amp;
                  \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{e}}
                  \\\
                  B \times B
                  \&amp;\stackrel{(-)\cdot (-)^{-1}}{\to}&amp;
                  B
                  }
                  \\,,
          %p where the bottom horizontal morphism is the composite
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo ×
                  %mi B
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi id
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi B
                  %mo ×
                  %mi B
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ⋅
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (-)\cdot (-)^{-1} : B \times B \stackrel{(id, (-)^{-1})}{\to} B \times B \stackrel{\cdot}{\to} B
          %p of a morphism that sends the second argument to its inverse with the group composition operation.
          %p
            It then follows by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
            and prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SequenceFromDiagonal"}
            that in this case the morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times_B Y \to X \times Y
            in the Mayer-Vietoris sequence is itself the homotopy fiber of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msup
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times Y \stackrel{f \cdot g^{-1}}{\longrightarrow} B
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ⋅
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                  %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega B \longrightarrow X \times_B Y \longrightarrow X \times Y
                  \\stackrel{f \cdot g^{-1}}{\longrightarrow} B
                  \\,.
          %p First consider two more concrete special cases.
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              be a small
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} = Sh_{(\infty,1)}(S)
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %p
              This is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presented
              by the projective
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi proj
                        %mo ,
                        %mi loc
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{C} \simeq ([S^{op}, sSet]_{proj, loc})^\circ
                    \\,.
            %p
              As discussed there, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
              prolongs to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ξ
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo ≤
                        %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sAb
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Xi :
                    [S^{op}, Ch_{\bullet \leq 0}(Ab)]_{proj}
                    \\to
                    [S^{op}, sAb]_{proj}
                    \\to
                    [S^{op}, sSet]_{proj}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Let then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \in \mathcal{C}
              be an object with a presentation in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^{op}, sSet]
              in the image of this
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ξ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Xi
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              also for this presentation, and hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo =
                    %mi Ξ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B = \Xi(\tilde B)
              for some presheaf of chain complexes
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde B
            %p
              We claim now that such
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              satisfies the above assumption.
            %p
              To see this, first notice that the evident morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo :
                    %mover
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo ×
                    %mover
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} - : \tilde B \times \tilde B \to \tilde B
              is degreewise an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi Ch
                        %mrow
                          %mo •
                          %mo ≥
                          %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Ab
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^{op}, Ch_{\bullet \geq 0}(Ab)]_{proj}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ξ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Xi
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} right Quillen
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} - : B \times B \to B
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^{op}, sSet]_{proj}
            %p Therefore the ordinary pullback of presheaves of chain complexes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi B
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi Δ
                                    %mover
                                      %mi B
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi B
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                            %mo ×
                            %mover
                              %mi B
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi B
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\tilde B &amp;\to&amp; *
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\Delta_{\tilde B}}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{0}}
                    \\\
                    \\tilde B \times \tilde B &amp;\stackrel{-}{\to}&amp; \tilde B
                    }
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi Ch
                        %mrow
                          %mo •
                          %mo ≥
                          %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Ab
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^{op}, Ch_{\bullet \geq 0}(Ab)]_{proj}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi Δ
                                    %mi B
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                            %mo ×
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    B &amp;\to&amp; *
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\Delta_B}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{0}}
                    \\\
                    B \times B &amp;\stackrel{-}{\to}&amp; B
                    }
            %p
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^{op}, sSet]_{proj}
            %p
              Since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stackification"} ∞-stackification
              preserves
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limits"} finite (∞,1)-limits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
              also in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          #SimplicialGroupObjectAsBase.num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              with a 1-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              of definition (a
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-localic+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} 1-localic (∞,1)-topos
            %p
              Then (as discussed there) every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
              object in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              has a presentation by a presheaf of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+groups"} simplicial groups
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sGrp
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    B \in [S^{op}, sGrp]_{proj} \to [S^{op}, sSet]_{proj}
                    \\,.
            %p
              We claim that the canonical morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} - : B \times B \to B
              is objectwise a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
              and hence a fibration in the projective
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in S
              be any test object. A diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Λ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi k
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi ha
                                %mo ,
                                %mi hb
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ×
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi j
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi σ
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\Lambda[k]^i &amp;\stackrel{(ha, hb)}{\to}&amp; B(U) \times B(U)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{j}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Delta[k] &amp;\stackrel{\sigma}{\to}&amp; B(U)
                    }
            %p
              corresponds to a
              = succeed "-cell" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma \in B(U)
              together with a choice of decomposition of the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi j
                      %mo *
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^* \sigma
              as a difference
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi j
                      %mo *
                    %mi σ
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi l
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi ha
                      %mi l
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msubsup
                      %mi hb
                      %mi l
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (j^* \sigma)_l = ha_l \cdot hb_l^{-1}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(U)
              itself is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
              (being a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \colon \Delta[k] \to B(U)
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi hb
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi Λ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi k
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi i
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hb \colon \Lambda[k]^i \to B(U)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi σ
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi b
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a \coloneqq \sigma \cdot b
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since all the face maps are group homomorphisms, this is indeed a filler of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ha
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ha
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi δ
                              %mi l
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
